# `InGameScreenshot` was a fourth line here until 2026-08-08. Its six sinks are
# `docs/mismatch/` now, so `docs` already covers them — one exception fewer.

# ── one exception, and it is about the code RUNNING, not about history ──
# The rule is "does a clean clone RUN", not "is it small". These trees are the
# TEMPLATES the detectors load at import — lobby tabs by glyph, weapon name
# plates, fire-mode / posture / type icons, the ADS crosshair. Without them a
# fresh checkout has no lobby chain (read_page returns None, so ensure_mode ->
# press_play -> ensure_in_match refuses to act), no weapon-name OCR and no
# posture. ~1 MB total, and NOT rebuildable: rebuilding needs a corpus that is
# itself ignored (and as of 2026-08-08 several of those corpora are deleted).
#
# ⚠ TWO THINGS THIS BLOCK GOT WRONG BEFORE 2026-08-08, both found by moving the
# tree under docs/ — a move is what forces every ignore rule to be re-applied,
# so it is the event that shows you what the rules were actually doing:
#
#   1. It said "these 24 files". `git ls-files` said 106, across ocr_white/,
#      pubg_assets/{fire_mode,posture,type,lobby}/ and lobby/tabs/ (36, not 24).
#   2. Only lobby/tabs/*.png was ever un-ignored. THE OTHER 70 WERE TRACKED BY
#      INERTIA — .gitignore does not apply to files already in the index, so
#      they had been added before the rules existed and simply never left.
#      Nothing would have re-added them; a clean clone kept working purely
#      because nobody had cause to re-add.
#
# So the rules now say what the index already contained, which is also what the
# stated criterion asks for. `git check-ignore -v <file>` names the winning rule
# when this needs debugging.
!docs/
docs/*
!docs/training_data/
docs/training_data/*
!docs/training_data/ocr_white/
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/
docs/training_data/pubg_assets/*
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/fire_mode/
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/posture/
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/type/
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/lobby/
docs/training_data/pubg_assets/lobby/*
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/lobby/tabs/
# ⚠ AND the files, explicitly. Re-including the DIRECTORY is not enough:
# line 10's `*.png` matches at every depth and would take them straight back
# out. Re-includes are per-rule, not per-tree — that is the second rule that
# has to be beaten.
!docs/training_data/ocr_white/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/fire_mode/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/posture/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/type/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/lobby/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/lobby/tabs/*.png
!docs/training_data/pubg_assets/*.npz

# (highlight_eval/ and weapon_hud_bank.npz stay OUT: 15 MB of labelled eval
#  corpus and a 2.9 MB PCA bank. The bank is derived — but ⚠ as of 2026-08-08
#  its corpus (Manual/weapon_hud, 128 MB) is DELETED, so "rebuild it with
#  calibration/build_weapon_hud_bank.py" is no longer true. It is now an
#  unrebuildable ignored file, which is the worst of both; if that matters,
#  the fix is to track it, not to pretend the corpus is coming back.)


